Chapter 5
Reading the Pattern
قراءة النمط
The three lenses of the last three chapters produce numbers. This chapter turns numbers into findings, and findings into decisions, which is what an analyst is paid for and what the exam means by analysing data to identify patterns that can be used to make business decisions.
A finding is not a calculation. "Cost of goods sold grew 17.2 per cent" is a calculation. "Cost of goods sold grew faster than sales in both years, which cost $850,080 of gross profit at this year's volume, and the cause is upstream of the factory" is a finding. The difference is that the second one can be acted on.
Figure F505-01 is your map.
Figure F505-01. Chapter 5 roadmap: from three lenses to one decision.
